.TH PABRIKON 1 "2026-10-17" "Pabrikon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pabrikon \- develop, validate, build, and package Linux icon themes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pabrikon
.I command
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pabrikon
is a Python command-line toolkit for developing Linux icon themes. It manages
project configuration, validates SVG sources and theme metadata, builds icon
variants, creates alias links, optimizes SVG files, and packages generated
themes.
.PP
Project configuration is stored at
.BR data/pabrikon.toml .
Source SVG files belong under
.B icons/<context>/scalable/ .
Generated theme files are written under
.IR build/ ,
and package archives are written under
.IR dist/ .
.SH INSTALLATION
Python 3.12 or newer is required. From a Pabrikon source checkout, install for
the current user with:
.nf
\&./install.sh
.fi
.PP
The installer places the environment under
.B ~/.local/share/pabrikon
and links the command from
.BR ~/.local/bin .
Add that directory to
.B PATH
if needed. The installer does not use sudo or modify shell startup files. A
pip installation is also available:
.nf
python3.12 -m pip install .
.fi
.PP
Install
.B rsvg-convert
from librsvg to render PNG icons and
.B svgcleaner
to optimize SVG files. The package installer does not install these system
tools.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [TARGET] [--name NAME]
Create a project in TARGET (default: current directory). Creates
.BR data/pabrikon.toml ,
.BR README.md ,
.BR index.theme ,
.BR data/aliases.toml ,
and the configured
.B icons/<context>/scalable/
directories. Existing project files are preserved; initialization fails if
.B data/pabrikon.toml
already exists.
If a root-level
.B pabrikon.toml
is found, move it to
.B data/pabrikon.toml
before initializing.
.TP
.B config edit [PATH] [--editor EDITOR]
Open an existing
.B data/pabrikon.toml
in a terminal editor. The file is not parsed before opening, so invalid TOML
can be repaired. If it is missing, run
.B pabrikon init
to create it. The editor is selected from
.BR --editor ,
.BR VISUAL ,
.BR EDITOR ,
.BR vim ,
then
.BR nano .
.TP
.B validate [PATH] [--json]
Check project configuration, source icons, theme metadata, aliases, and
generated output. PATH defaults to the current directory. The
.B --json
option prints machine-readable diagnostics.
.TP
.B build [PATH] [OPTIONS]
Build configured SVG and PNG variants in
.BR build/ .
The output includes a build-ready
.BR index.theme .
Unchanged outputs may be reused.
.TP
.B clean [PATH] [--type TYPE] [--dry-run]
Remove generated files from
.BR build/ .
TYPE may be
.BR build ,
.BR png ,
.BR svg ,
or
.BR symlink ;
the default is
.BR build .
Source files under
.B icons/
are not removed. Use
.B --dry-run
to list the files that would be removed.
.TP
.B aliases edit [PATH] [--editor EDITOR]
Open
.B data/aliases.toml
in a terminal editor. If the file is missing, a commented example template is
created before opening it. The editor is selected from
.BR --editor ,
.BR VISUAL ,
.BR EDITOR ,
.BR vim ,
then
.BR nano .
.TP
.B aliases build [PATH] [--dry-run]
Create symbolic links in
.B build/
from alias definitions in
.BR data/aliases.toml .
.TP
.B optimize [PATH] [--dry-run] [--in-place]
Optimize source SVG files using
.BR svgcleaner .
By default, optimized copies are written below
.BR dist/optimized/icons/ .
With
.BR --in-place ,
validated optimized files replace their sources. Use
.B --dry-run
to preview the operation.
.TP
.B package [PATH] [--dry-run]
Create a deterministic
.B .tar.gz
archive in
.B dist/
from a successfully built and validated theme. The dry-run option validates
the package inputs without creating an archive.
.TP
.B info [PATH] [--json]
Show project metadata and icon counts. The
.B --json
option prints JSON.
.TP
.B list [KIND] [PATH] [--json]
List icons, directories, aliases, or generated files. KIND defaults to
.BR icons .
.TP
.B theme init [PATH] [--force]
Generate the root
.B index.theme
from
.BR data/pabrikon.toml .
An existing file is preserved unless
.B --force
is supplied.
.TP
.B theme show [PATH]
Print the effective theme metadata.
.TP
.B theme edit [PATH] [--editor EDITOR]
Open the project's root
.B index.theme
in a terminal editor. If the file is missing, it is generated from
.B data/pabrikon.toml
before opening. The editor is selected from
.BR --editor ,
.BR VISUAL ,
.BR EDITOR ,
.BR vim ,
then
.BR nano .
.TP
.B theme validate [PATH]
Validate
.B index.theme
against the project configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed Pabrikon version.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Show per-file details where the command provides them.
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Suppress normal text output; errors remain visible on standard error.
.TP
.B --debug
Show a traceback for unexpected errors.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Preview supported changes without writing generated output. Availability is
command-specific; see the command help.
.TP
.B --all
Rebuild every output even if it is up to date (build only).
.TP
.B --size N
Build one configured raster size.
.TP
.B --sizes N,N,...
Build a comma-separated set of configured raster sizes.
.TP
.B --directory DIR
Build only one configured icon context.
.TP
.B --icon NAME
Build only the named icon. NAME may be an icon name or CONTEXT/NAME.
.TP
.B --type TYPE
Select generated files for clean: build, png, svg, or symlink.
.TP
.B --in-place
Replace source SVGs with validated optimized results (optimize only).
.TP
.B --json
Print one machine-readable JSON value. Available for all commands, including
nested commands. Errors are reported as JSON and preserve the command exit
code. JSON output is written even when --quiet is also specified.
.TP
.B --editor EDITOR
Select the command used by
.BR theme edit
,
.BR aliases edit ,
or
.BR config edit .
The value may include arguments, such as
.BR "nano --linenumbers" .
It is parsed as an argument list and is not run through a shell.
.SH PROJECT LAYOUT
.nf
my-theme/
|-- README.md
|-- index.theme
|-- icons/                    editable source files
|   |-- apps/scalable/*.svg
|   |-- places/scalable/*.svg
|   `-- ...
|-- data/
|   |-- pabrikon.toml         project configuration
|   `-- aliases.toml          optional
|-- build/                    generated by pabrikon build
|   |-- index.theme
|   |-- apps/scalable/*.svg
|   `-- apps/48x48/*.png
`-- dist/                     packages and optimized copies
.fi
.PP
Each enabled context in
.B build.directories.enabled
has a source directory at
.B icons/<context>/scalable/ .
Raster sizes and output formats are configured in
.BR data/pabrikon.toml .
The
.B build/
directory is created by the first build and can be regenerated without
changing the source tree.
.SH EXISTING PROJECTS
Pabrikon can be used manually with an existing icon-theme checkout. If
.B data/pabrikon.toml
does not exist, run
.B pabrikon init
with the actual theme root; some repositories store the theme in a nested
directory. Initialization preserves existing files and creates missing
Pabrikon starter files, but does not infer configuration or rearrange assets.
.PP
Copy original scalable SVGs into
.B icons/<context>/scalable/
for each enabled context. For example:
.nf
mkdir -p /path/to/theme-root/icons/apps/scalable
find /path/to/theme-root/ExistingTheme/apps/scalable -type f -name '*.svg' \\
  -exec cp -p {} /path/to/theme-root/icons/apps/scalable/ \\\\;
.fi
.PP
Adjust the source path for the theme and repeat for each context. Check for
duplicate SVG basenames first; the target context is flat, so same-named files
would overwrite each other. Copy rather than move the files so the original
layout remains intact. Edit
.B data/pabrikon.toml
with
.BR "pabrikon config edit /path/to/theme-root" .
If that file already exists, edit it instead of running init again. If a
Pabrikon config is at the repository root, move it to
.B data/pabrikon.toml
before initialization. Review the config and existing
.B index.theme
before building. To replace an existing
.B index.theme
from the config, explicitly use
.BR "pabrikon theme init /path/to/theme-root --force" .
.PP
Pabrikon does not yet discover nested theme roots, infer settings from an
upstream
.BR index.theme ,
import raster assets, or normalize the repository layout automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a project:
.B pabrikon init my-theme
.TP
Validate, build, and package it:
.br
.B pabrikon validate my-theme
.br
.B pabrikon build my-theme
.br
.B pabrikon package my-theme
.TP
Preview generated-file cleanup:
.B pabrikon clean my-theme --dry-run
.TP
Validate the current project:
.B pabrikon validate .
.TP
Preview a 48-pixel build:
.B pabrikon build . --size 48 --dry-run
.TP
Build all configured sizes:
.B pabrikon build .
.TP
Remove generated files after previewing the operation:
.br
.B pabrikon clean . --dry-run
.br
.B pabrikon clean .
.TP
Optimize SVGs without replacing sources:
.B pabrikon optimize .
.TP
Package a completed theme:
.B pabrikon package .
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Python 3.12 or newer is required. The
.B rsvg-convert
program (provided by librsvg) is required to render PNG icons. The
.B svgcleaner
program is required to optimize SVG files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Validation or execution failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments or configuration.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Automatic project analysis and layout normalization are not implemented yet;
see
.BR "EXISTING PROJECTS" .
Pabrikon v2 uses
.B data/aliases.toml
instead of the legacy CSV alias tables and does not import external CSV maps.
Browser preview is not currently available.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsvg-convert (1),
.BR svgcleaner (1)
